Why is this the lexicographically smallest?

Suppose the frequencies are:

a : 2
b : 2
c : 2

Possible left halves are:

abc
acb
bac
bca
cab
cba

These generate different palindromes:

abccba
acbbca
baccab
...

The smallest is the one whose left half is alphabetically smallest, i.e., "abc". Since the first differing character determines lexicographic order, placing the smallest available letters in the left half as early as possible guarantees the smallest overall palindrome. That's why the loop processes characters from 'a' to 'z' and appends freq[i] / 2 copies of each.
